          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How does the electronics recycling process work?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "The Bakersfield electronics recycling process begins with equipment and scheduling information, followed by pickup coordination, documented transport, sorting, data destruction or reuse evaluation, material recovery, and project reporting. STS organizes each step around clear communication, asset information, and chain-of-custody documentation."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How does STS document electronics disposition?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "STS documents electronics disposition through available asset records, pickup information, data destruction documentation, chain-of-custody records, and final disposition reporting. Bakersfield organizations can identify documentation requirements during planning so the project file reflects the equipment, services, and reporting needs involved."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What certifications and standards are relevant?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Relevant documentation for Bakersfield electronics projects may reference NIST 800-88, HIPAA safeguards, ISO 27001 controls, or DoD 5220.22-M practices depending on the equipment and customer requirements. STS can discuss applicable records during planning rather than applying one standard to every load."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What areas does STS serve?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "STS serves Bakersfield, Kern County, and organizations across the Central Valley through scheduled commercial pickup. Businesses and institutions can share their Bakersfield project location, equipment types, approximate volume, and timing so the team can recommend an appropriate logistics plan."
          }
        },
